  "note": "A1+ Unit 1 Lesson 1.7 rebuilt on 2026-11-12 under the A1+ lesson standards approved 2026-10-27 and the user's 2026-11-09 rule that every A1+ lesson follows up the A1 lesson with the same number. A1 1.7 Family Actions shows people playing, studying, working, cooking and talking (The father is working.). A1+ 1.7 turns two of those actions into habits and asks about them: How often do you study at night? / How often do you work at home?, built from A1 4.8's Do you work? / Do you study? and answered with 1.6's frequency words in the I-form. The narrator reports each answer with he/she -s, which brings the -ies spelling (Diego usually studies at night.) next to the plain -s (Sofia always works at home.). Facts: Diego usually studies at night (at his desk at home), Ana sometimes studies at night (in a library, so her photo never shows her at home), Sofia always works at home (she writes books, A1+ 1.2) and Luis never works at home (he drives a bus, as in A1 3.9). Ana asks Diego and Luis; Luis asks Ana and Sofia (Ana and Sofia share one voice, as do Luis and Diego). Frequency cannot be photographed: each photo shows who does what, the Listen text cards set the frequency words against each other, and a never sentence never meets a photo that does not contradict it.",
